@startuml
title Sequence diagram: Safety Officer records the outcome
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

' People work in the Web App, which calls the Backend API with their login token, so
' every call and its answer is two arrows: person <-> Web App, Web App <-> Backend API.
' Only the arrows to and from the Backend API and PostgreSQL are numbered, as in the
' draw.io and PDF versions.
' A notification is a record saved in PostgreSQL. Nothing is pushed to its recipient
' (no email, websocket or polling): the Web App fetches it later with
' GET /api/notifications, as the last section shows.

actor "Event\nCoordinator" as coordinator
actor "Safety\nOfficer" as safety
participant "Web App\n(React)" as web
participant "Backend API" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

== Safety Officer records the outcome (the event must be in Safety Review) ==
alt Approved
  safety -> web : Approve
  autonumber
  web -> api : POST /api/events/requests/:reference/safety-outcome
  api -> db : Record approval:\nthe event stays in Safety Review
  api -> db : Save notification: coordinator
  api --> web : The request, still in Safety Review
  autonumber stop
  web --> safety : Show the result
else Rejected or changes requested
  safety -> web : Reject or request changes
  autonumber resume
  web -> api : POST /api/events/requests/:reference/safety-outcome
  api -> db : Status returns to approved,\nback to planning
  api -> db : If named: flag venue\narrangements, reopen\nequipment lines
  api -> db : Save notification: coordinator,\nwith the reason
  api -> db : Save notification: Venue Staff,\nTechnical Support (if named)
  api --> web : The request, back in planning
  autonumber stop
  web --> safety : Show the result
end

== Later, the Web App fetches the coordinator's saved notifications (nothing is pushed) ==
coordinator -> web : Open notifications
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/notifications
api --> web : The safety outcome and its reason
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show notifications
@enduml
